sizu-writer Repository Version History
======================================

v2.0.0 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Replace the OpenAI specific environment variables with provider neutral
  generation settings. Using the openai package as a client and talking to
  OpenAI the company are separate facts, and only the first is true by
  default; the settings, the module names and the log lines now say so.
- Require an explicit backend, token, base URL and model, so that no
  endpoint is ever selected implicitly. A blank base URL used to mean
  OpenAI, which let a deployment address a service without naming it.
  Validation runs when app.py is imported and before a CLI subcommand, so
  a worker that cannot reach an endpoint refuses to start rather than
  accepting a memo and failing on the request.
- Add sizu_writer/providers/, holding everything that knows how an
  endpoint is spoken to: the SDK, the authentication, the base URL, the
  request shape and the client's exceptions. generator.py now works from a
  CompletionResult, so a second wire protocol can be added as a module and
  a registry entry without touching what a body and its titles have to
  look like.
- Support Sakura AI Engine account tokens, of the form <UUID>:<secret>,
  against its OpenAI compatible Chat Completions API. sizu-writer now runs
  with no OpenAI account at all, and Sakura AI Engine is not built in as a
  backend of its own: it is reached as what it is, an explicitly configured
  OpenAI compatible endpoint.
- Add the json-object and prompt-json response modes. prompt-json is the
  default and sends no response_format, so an endpoint or a model that
  rejects the parameter still answers; it additionally accepts an object
  wrapped in a single code fence. Neither mode extracts an object out of
  surrounding prose, because that heuristic is what lets an opening remark
  become the first line of a post. There is no automatic mode: trying one
  and retrying with the other would make one generation cost two requests.
- Default the API retries to zero, so that one screen action or one CLI run
  spends one request. On a plan counting requests, an unpredictable
  multiplier is expensive, and the retries the SDK would have spent are the
  least visible part of the total.
- Never fall back to a second endpoint. One generation uses one route, so
  which service received the memo, which model replied, how many requests
  were spent and whose failure ended the run all stay answerable.
- Log the shape of each exchange and none of its content: the backend, the
  endpoint host, the request id, the model, the finish reason and the token
  counts, with a matching line naming the HTTP status of a failure. The
  token, the memo, the prompts, the body and the titles appear at no level.
- Refuse the legacy OPENAI_* settings and an unknown backend before any
  request is made, naming the setting at fault and never quoting a secret.
  There is no translation, no aliasing and no precedence rule, so a stale
  OPENAI_API_KEY exported in a shell cannot decide where a memo is sent.
- Document the generation path in doc/DETAILED_DESIGN_GENERATION_API.md,
  and update the README, the basic design, the deployment guide, the prompt
  document and doc/POLICY to match. The README covers choosing an endpoint,
  the two response modes, the request budget and the upgrade from v1.x.

v1.0.0 (Release Date: 2026-08-04)
---------------------------------
- Initial release. A Flask application that turns a short memo into a
  post body and title candidates for Shizuka na Internet, with the
  generation core (sizu_writer/) kept independent from the web layer so
  that cli.py can settle the prompts before any screen is involved.
- The prompts live in prompts/*.md, outside the Python package, so that
  adjusting the writing policy needs neither a code change nor a
  reinstall.
- The server keeps no state: the memo and the current body travel with
  the form, which is what lets the titles be regenerated without a
  session store.
- The repository is written in English throughout, including the
  screens, the documents and the prompts. Only the generated post is
  Japanese, because the medium is. The Japanese that remains in the
  source is load bearing: the phrases formatter.py matches against a
  generated body, the fixtures that exercise it, and the openings and
  closings quoted in the prompts and the specifications as the literal
  strings the model must not produce. The screens are marked lang="en",
  with lang="ja" on the elements carrying the memo and the draft.
- Documented to the level of id774/ai-digest: a README covering the
  concept, installation, every setting, both entry points, the notices,
  the failures and the deployment, plus doc/PROMPTS.md for the prompt
  layer, which is where the quality of the output actually lives.
- OPENAI_TEMPERATURE is validated like every other numeric setting, so
  a bad value is refused by name instead of raising a bare float error.
- Not implemented yet, and deliberately left for a later change: the
  space inserted between full width characters and ASCII, the
  json_schema and none response format modes, the Origin check on POST,
  and LOG_PAYLOAD. PROMPT_RELOAD is absent for a different reason: it
  was to switch off a cache, and no cache was built, so the prompts are
  read on every generation already.
- Return a safe HTTP 413 response when a submitted request exceeds the
  server limit, without parsing the oversized form again.
